WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.152
Common table expressions are mainly a query-organization tool.

00:00:04.152 --> 00:00:12.082
Postgres can sometimes inline or fold a non-recursive common table expression into the surrounding query.

00:00:12.082 --> 00:00:16.687
In other situations, materialization behavior can matter.

00:00:16.687 --> 00:00:22.917
The practical lesson for this course is simple: use common table expressions for clarity,

00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:26.812
and inspect the execution plan when performance matters.

00:00:26.812 --> 00:00:32.191
Do not assume that using a common table expression automatically makes a query faster.
